message: "If you use adaptiveNet in academic, teaching, or published work, please cite it using the metadata below. The DOI under `doi:` always resolves to the latest version; pin to a specific version via the `identifiers:` block."
title: adaptiveNet
abstract: >-
  An interactive browser-based playground for node-edge dynamical systems
  where node states and connection topology coevolve. Includes Hopfield
  memory, spiking neurons, Ising spins, reaction-diffusion, voter dynamics,
  and self-organised criticality as instances of one substrate.
